{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Until the ninth year.</b> Until the festival of Sukkot of the ninth year, which is the time when the produce of the eighth year comes into the house — for all the days of summer they were in the field, at the threshing floors, and in Tishrei is the time of gathering into the house. And sometimes it required a four-year supply — in the sixth year, before the seventh sabbatical year — when they are barred from working the land for two consecutive years, the seventh and the Jubilee. And this verse is stated regarding all the other sabbatical years."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:17.965695910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}